Z||000001||Monkeyman||02-07-2001||12:32 AM||||Ummm...That has got to be the ugliest MH I've ever seen.  Interesting idea, but you wouldn't see that in my driveway.  I can't believe someone spent over a quarter of a million bucks to develop that.  For that kind of money, you'd think they would have had the sense to hire someone with some taste.  On a positive note, I'll bet one of those captains chairs would make a great office chair. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||02-07-2001||05:17 AM||||Looks to me like there would be so much drag from the wheels that it would be difficult to get over 5 knots in the water, if that. <P>A few years ago I saw a oddly futuristic motorhome back down a boat ramp at Lake Martin. I thought at first they were going to load a boat, but I noticed there was no trailer. They backed the rear wheels well into the water and a portion of the motorhome seperated along a decrative stripe and slid off the chassis to become a house boat. There was access between the remaining cab and the boat when it was in use as a motorhome. It appeared to be manufactured but I,ve seen nothing like it before or since. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||02-07-2001||06:19 PM||||That thing is strange looking but kinda neat. Boston has Amphibious duck tours. It kinda looks like that thing. It starts on land then drives into the harbor and continues a tour of the city. It is a military vehicle that was used in WW2. look at this <A HREF="http://www.ducktours.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ducktours.com</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.ducktours.com/media/montag2a.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A><p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 02-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Hank is Here||02-07-2001||09:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TheFiero64:<BR><B>That thing is strange looking but kinda neat. Boston has Amphibious duck tours. It kinda looks like that thing. It starts on land then drives into the harbor and continues a tour of the city. It is a military vehicle that was used in WW2. look at this<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ducks are some of the coolest vehicles ever made.  They were called DUKW, they were made my GMC.  The heck of it was they were designed in just under one month, amazing by todays standards, granted they did start with a spec deuce or CCKW.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||02-08-2001||12:13 AM||||On the next episode of the A-team:<P>See what happens when a group of retirees kidnaps the A-team and locks them up overnight in RV/Campers World.  <P>B.A. : "I pity da fool who dont like my RV."<BR>Hannibal: "Beautiful, I love it when a plan comes together."<P><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000006||stimpy||02-08-2001||12:56 AM||||Out where this uh, thing is located is bigtime delta country with the tendency to flood every other year or so.  Not to mention there are lots and lots and lots of islands in all those rivers.  I think it would be a blast to drive into the river and up on to some island for camping.  Lost Isle, anyone?  (ur2biteme should know what I'm talking about.) ||||reg||1
